From 6973fdccc457edf4dc502e4230d0db860fa15be9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:42:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] virt: gunyah: report the VM status when a vCPU of an
 exiting VM is re-entered

A protected VM that powers off through PSCI SYSTEM_OFF exits from the
vCPU run loop only after the resource manager's VM_EXITED notification
has set vm_status. The resource manager stops the VM's vCPUs before
that notification arrives; a vCPU thread woken in between (wakeup VIRQ)
re-enters gunyah_hypercall_vcpu_run() and gets an error, which
GUNYAH_VCPU_RUN returned to the VMM instead of the EXITED status. Seen
as one of five power-off runs on a OnePlus Pad 4 without an EXITED
status (reasoned from the code; the run's output was not kept).

On a hypercall error, wait up to 500 ms for vm_status to leave RUNNING
and report the VM status as GUNYAH_VCPU_EXIT_STATUS if it did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_vcpu.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_vcpu.c b/drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_vcpu.c
index 0dd3569a5645..1fcadc377010 100644
--- a/drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_vcpu.c
+++ b/drivers/virt/gunyah/gunyah_vcpu.c
@@ -409,6 +409,22 @@ static int gunyah_vcpu_run(struct gunyah_vcpu *vcpu)
 			schedule();
 		} else {
 			ret = gunyah_error_remap(gunyah_error);
+			/*
+			 * The resource manager stops the vCPUs of an exiting VM
+			 * before its VM_EXITED notification reaches us. A vCPU
+			 * woken in between (wakeup VIRQ) re-enters the hypercall
+			 * and gets an error: wait briefly for the notification
+			 * and report the VM status instead of the error.
+			 */
+			if (wait_event_interruptible_timeout(
+				    vcpu->ghvm->vm_status_wait,
+				    READ_ONCE(vcpu->ghvm->vm_status) !=
+					    GUNYAH_RM_VM_STATUS_RUNNING,
+				    msecs_to_jiffies(500)) > 0 &&
+			    !gunyah_vcpu_check_system(vcpu)) {
+				ret = 0;
+				goto out;
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
